# p_e5f6 — The Shared Breakfast Table; Hana Packs Lunch, Priya Does Light Dinners

Both residents cook together for breakfast on weekdays (7:00–7:45): Hana makes toast and eggs, Priya pours tea. They eat at the dining table. Hana then packs a lunchbox and works from home at desk_b1 until 12:30. She leaves at 13:40 with her tablet, a sandwich, and her water bottle. Priya cooks a light lunch for herself at 12:30. In the afternoon Priya does errands 14:00–15:30. At 18:00 Priya makes a simple dinner (soup, salad) for both—Hana eats when she gets home at 23:00, or it's reheated. Evening: they watch TV together 23:15–00:15, then Hana plays guitar 00:15–01:00, Priya reads until 22:30 (she goes to bed before Hana returns on weekdays, so the TV is really just for Hana on weeknights). On weekends they have a proper brunch 10:30–12:00, Hana does errands 13:00–15:00, and they play a board game 19:00–20:30.

What sets this apart: the puzzle_box moves to the dining table on weekends 19:00–20:30. The cooking items (pan, knife, cutting board) are at the counter 7:00–7:45 weekdays (shared breakfast). Hana's notebook is at desk_b1 all morning.

What would refute it: puzzle_box_shared found at bookshelf_l1 at 19:30 on a Saturday; kitchen_knife_shared found at drawer_k_k1 at 7:15 on a weekday; notebook_hana found at nightstand_b1 at 9:00 on a weekday.

